  "worked_solution": "We use the Euclidean algorithm, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}296 & = & 185(1) & + & 111 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 185 & = & 111(1) & + & 74 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 111 & = & 74(1) & + & 37 \\\\  & ↙ &  & ↙ &  \\\\ 74 & = & 37(2) & + & 0\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe last positive remainder is $37.$ Therefore, we conclude that the greatest common divisor of $296$ and $185$ is $37.$ Symbolically, we write\n\n$$\n\\text{gcd}(296,185)=37.\n$$",
